WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 5.2 · Internal Systems & Operations
Minimum viable systems by stage

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Build the few systems you need to start, and know what will trigger the next ones.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:26.652
Minimum viable systems are the fewest systems that keep your work safe and organised at your current stage. Each stage keeps what came before and adds only what its new risks require.

4
00:00:27.052 --> 00:00:27.652
What each stage adds

5
00:00:27.652 --> 00:00:40.093
Idea stage: Group chat, shared folder, cash book with receipts, a decisions note and consent forms. For example: Two founders testing the bakery keep receipts in one envelope and decisions in one note.

6
00:00:40.093 --> 00:00:52.163
Early delivery: Bank account in the organisation's name, two signatories, simple bookkeeping, agreements and a leave record. For example: The bakery opens its own account once the first café pays an invoice.

7
00:00:52.163 --> 00:01:06.174
Growing team: Accounting software, approval limits, process owners, a planning calendar and restricted personnel files. For example: With its own shop and staff, the bakery adds approval limits and an owner for every process.

8
00:01:06.574 --> 00:01:07.174
Why proportionate matters

9
00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:12.107
1. Too few systems put people and money at risk.

10
00:01:12.107 --> 00:01:17.041
2. Too many waste scarce time on tools nobody maintains.

11
00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:24.085
3. Written triggers turn each next step into a decision, not a crisis.

12
00:01:24.485 --> 00:01:25.085
How you will use it

13
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:31.130
1. Your launch list: the minimum you need before or soon after launch.

14
00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:37.174
2. Your triggers: registering, a bank account, the first employee or restricted funding.

15
00:01:37.174 --> 00:01:43.848
3. Your budget and policies in later modules, added as triggers appear.

16
00:01:44.248 --> 00:01:44.848
What to avoid

17
00:01:44.848 --> 00:01:48.670
Wanting everything perfect before you start.

18
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:53.604
Procedures nobody reads and records kept in two places.

19
00:01:53.604 --> 00:02:01.019
Ignoring a trigger, such as first work with children, until something goes wrong.

20
00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:03.419
You define your minimum systems and the triggers for adding more.

21
00:02:03.419 --> 00:02:07.419
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:08.919 --> 00:02:12.019
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
